description:
## Scope

New module `src/dispatch/tmux.rs`. Pure tmux wrapper — no claude-specific logic. The single primitive every higher layer composes on.

## API

```rust
pub struct TmuxSpawn { session: String, worktree: PathBuf }

impl TmuxSpawn {
    /// Create a detached session named `rsry-<session_id>` rooted in worktree.
    /// Errors loudly if tmux not installed or session already exists.
    pub fn new(session_id: &str, worktree: &Path) -> Result<Self>;

    /// Look up an existing session by id; None if not present.
    pub fn attach(session_id: &str) -> Result<Option<Self>>;

    /// Send a command to the session (tmux send-keys ... Enter).
    pub fn send(&self, command: &str) -> Result<()>;

    /// Capture full pane scrollback as a string. Pass start_line for incremental capture.
    pub fn capture(&self, start_line: Option<i64>) -> Result<String>;

    /// True iff tmux has-session reports the session exists.
    pub fn is_alive(&self) -> Result<bool>;

    /// tmux kill-session. Idempotent — no error if already gone.
    pub fn kill(self) -> Result<()>;
}
```

## Acceptance

- `TmuxSpawn::new()` creates a detached session, returns the wrapper. Real tmux on the test machine.
- Session name is exactly `rsry-<session_id>`. Convention pinned by ADR-0011.
- `new()` errors cleanly with `"tmux not installed; brew install tmux"` when which-tmux fails.
- `new()` errors cleanly when session-already-exists (don't silently re-use).
- `attach()` returns None for missing sessions, Some(_) for existing, idempotent.
- `send()` writes a command and the trailing Enter.
- `capture()` returns the pane scrollback. Empty string is valid (fresh session, no output).
- `is_alive()` returns true for live sessions, false after kill, false if tmux server is down.
- `kill()` is idempotent.

## Tests (TDD, 8-10)

- `new_creates_session_with_canonical_name`
- `new_fails_when_tmux_missing` (mock PATH)
- `new_fails_when_session_already_exists`
- `attach_returns_none_for_missing_session`
- `send_and_capture_roundtrip` (send `echo hello`, capture finds "hello")
- `is_alive_false_after_kill`
- `kill_is_idempotent`
- `parallel_new_creates_isolated_sessions` (2 sessions, 2 worktrees, capture each)
- `capture_with_start_line_returns_incremental` (advanced — defer if scope tight)

All tests cleanly skip when `which tmux` fails — same pattern as the Dolt sandbox tests.

## Files

- `src/dispatch/tmux.rs` (new, ~250 lines incl. tests)
- `src/dispatch/mod.rs` (add `pub mod tmux;`)

## Risk surface

- **tmux output format varies across versions**: target tmux 3.0+ (universally available on macOS Homebrew + Linux distros from 2020+). Pin version check in `new()`.
- **macOS/Linux only**: Windows users would need WSL. Existing rosary dispatch already assumes Unix shape.
- **Real tmux in tests is slow**: each test ~50-200ms. Use a `#[ignore]` flag for slow tests if it bites, but try real-tmux first.

## Time-box

M — 1-2 days incl. tests.

## Depends on

- W0 (ADR-0011) — wait for design merge before implementing.

